## SQ-PS15B-12
@group A
@commands Reload test per switch (needs `/cdevreload compat`): save each with `sed -i` (rename, missed by the watcher), then run the command: `[debug.passthrough] timing` true / false, cobweb `denseWalk` 0.2, `breakStallTicks` 0, cobweb `surroundedAt` 3, layers `snowMaxSlow` 0.3, layers `minLayers` 4; also one save written in place (single write) without the command
@pass each value applies after the command (timing lines start / stop, speeds change, the client gets the re-sent table: no rubber band); the in-place save applies within a few seconds without the command
@fails `CompatConfigReload.reload`, `PassValues.onConfig` re-send; night-config watcher (ENTRY_MODIFY, count 1 only)
@reviewed 2026-11-17
# With the Creative Common build of 2026-11-17 (G11 own config watcher) each save here is also reloaded by Common about
# 1 s later (one `[creativecommon] creativecompat-common.toml reloaded` line per save), so the in-place step at the end
# passes on Common alone; the save-without-command checks live in SQ-PS15B-26.
# every switch is saved by a whole-file rewrite (qrun.py toml), which the watcher misses, then /cdevreload compat;
# the server copy is restored at the end. Cross web at 1000 -60 1200 (3 faces: dense), zombie z12x in it
shell cp config/creativecompat-common.toml .ps15b12_compat.toml
