## SQ-PS15B-14 | layersFall off, piston, chunk reload, fodder
@group A
@commands (a) `layersFall = false` (rename + `/cdevreload compat`): a snow 3 over a removed stone breaks as vanilla (no falling entity), fodder 4 stays floating; back to true. (b) a piston pushes a salt layer 4 off a stone ledge over a 3-deep gap: it falls and lands. (c) a floating snow 4 written into an unloaded chunk (`/setblock` then `/forceload remove` and reload) falls on its first random tick (randomTickSpeed 300)
@pass (a) no `creativecompat:falling_layer` entity, snow gone, fodder still at its height; (b) the salt layer at the gap bottom; (c) the snow on the ground within 20 s
@fails `FallingLayers.enabled`, `SuppFodderFallMixin`, piston `Block.updateFromNeighbourShapes` path, `SnowLayerFallMixin` randomTick
@draft steps to write at the run (needs the piston fixture and a chunk unload/reload sequence)

## SQ-PS15B-15 | full bamboo leaves by hand and drops; grown bamboo drops bamboo leaves
@group A
@commands Bot P uses Twigs bamboo leaves on a 4-layer pile 4 times (5, 6, 7, 8; a 5th use does nothing), then breaks it; bamboo: a 6-tall grown stalk (`age=1,stage=1`, top two `leaves=large`) with `bambooLeafChance 1.0` (rename + reload) and randomTickSpeed 300 for 10 s
@pass `creativecompat:bamboo_leaves_full[layers=8]` after 4 uses, pick block gives Twigs bamboo leaves, breaking drops 8 Twigs bamboo leaves; bamboo leaves appear on the ground beside the stalk, never more than 4 layers each (bambooLeafMaxLayers), none on a side blocked by a block; restore 0.0005
@fails `TwigsBambooLeavesMixin` canBeReplaced / getStateForPlacement, `FullBambooLeavesBlock.getDrops`, `BambooLeafDropMixin` (isRandomlyTicking needs the chunk loaded after the change: forceload the area after the reload), `BambooLeafDrops.land`
@draft pbot use sequence and the drop count readback to write at the run

## SQ-PS15B-16 | jump and fall inside layers: snow 5 vs 6, leaf pile 4 vs 5, fall cap
@group A
@commands Bot P jumps (pbot jump) from inside snow 5 and snow 6, an oak leaf pile 4 and 5, plain ground; per-tick Y watch. Drop P from 10 blocks into a 7-layer snow pile and an 8-layer leaf pile: per-tick motion Y inside
@pass jump apex above the start: plain about 1.25, snow 5 about 1.25, snow 6 about 0.63, leaf 4 about 1.25, leaf 5 about 1.05 (still onto a 1-block step beside it); inside the piles the fall speed is at most 0.12 (snow) and 0.24 (leaves) blocks per tick
@fails `LayerJumpMixin` (getJumpPower), `PassResult.addLayer`, `PassThrough.apply` capFall; exempt mobs and players in leather boots on top have no cell
@draft needs a pbot jump verb and a per-tick Y readback (zpth watch on the bot)

## SQ-PS15B-17 | leaf thorns: full pile 8 pricks a walking player; piles 6 and 7 only a sprinting one; pile 5 never; full armor never; creative never
@group A
@commands Bot P walks back and forth (pbot moveto) for 30 s in an 8-layer oak leaf pile with no armor, 2 armor pieces, 4 pieces; then walks, then sprints, 30 s each in a 6-layer and a 7-layer pile (no armor); then sneaks in the 8-layer pile; then a 5-layer pile sprinting; then creative; a fox, a rabbit and a cat in an 8-layer pile
@pass pile 8, no armor, walking: about 0.25 pricks per second (half a heart, death message of the berry bush kind); 2 pieces about half that; 4 pieces none; piles 6 and 7: walking none, sprinting about 0.25 per second; sneaking in pile 8 none; pile 5 none; creative none; the fox, rabbit and cat take no damage and are not slowed (`passthrough_exempt/layers`)
@fails `LeafThorns.onPlayerTick` (tick-to-tick speed over the pile's own walk factor), `LayerMotion.thornPrick` / `thornNeed` (`thornMinSpeed` 1.0 full, `thornPartialMinSpeed` 1.3 partial, the sprint flag), `LayerMotion.thornChance`, entity tag `creativecompat:passthrough_exempt/layers`
@draft health readback per second and the armor swaps to write at the run (Immersive Weathering's own spruce thorns also hurt in spruce piles: use oak); rewritten 2026-11-17 for G11 (was: piles 6 and 8 prick a walking player)

## SQ-PS15B-18 | mobs do not path through leaf piles of 6 or more
@group A
@commands A zombie and an MCA villager behind a 1-wide gap filled with an oak leaf pile, target 10 blocks beyond (a player for the zombie, `/mca` home or a bed for the villager): pile 6, then pile 5
@pass pile 6: neither paths through the gap (goes around if there is a way, else stays); pile 5: both walk through
@fails `LeafPilePathMixin` (WalkNodeEvaluator getBlockPathTypeRaw -> DAMAGE_OTHER), `McaLeafPilePathMixin`, `pathBlockLayers`
@draft path readback to write at the run (watch the mob's position for 20 s)

## SQ-PS15B-19 | 200 snow layers falling at once: TPS
@group A
@commands A 20 x 10 stone slab 6 above the ground with snow 3 on top, the stone removed in one /fill
@pass every pile lands (200 merged or placed piles, no snow left floating); mspt during the fall under 50
@fails `FallingLayers.onLevelTick` queue (512 per tick), entity count
@draft perf row (spark or the perf suite); steps at the run

## SQ-PS15B-20 | Devtools boots without Compat (second boot of SQ-TX-18)
@group A
@commands A boot with Creative Compat and every jar that requires it (Engineering, Calendar, Equipment, Delight, Brewing, Loot, Magic, Worldgen) removed from `OUT/srv/mods/`, Devtools and Common kept: `cdevreload compat`, `cdevbench passthrough`, `dumpsurface`, `cdevtest help`
@pass the server starts; no ERROR or NoClassDefFoundError naming `creativecompat`; the three Compat commands are `Unknown or incomplete command`; `cdevtest help` works
@fails Devtools mods.toml `creativecompat mandatory=false`, the `ModList.isLoaded("creativecompat")` guards in CreativeDevtools, SurfaceAudit, WthitIconDump
@draft a boot with a cut-down mod set; the qrun boot profile has no jar-removal step yet

## SQ-PS15B-21 | /cdevbench passthrough, 14 cases: first in its cells on saved counts, recount cases unbudgeted
@group A
@commands As SQ-PTH-25c with this Devtools build: `/cdevbench passthrough` twice
@pass `tick_field` and `tick_web_cube` under 1000 ns median (the per-tick table cleared, the chunk counts kept); `tick_field_recount` and `tick_web_cube_recount` recorded (full recount, no budget, white in chat); record all 14 in blockrunner.md 3.10
@fails `PassBenchCommand.cold` (`PassCountCache.at` with a fresh key), `recount` (`PassCountCache.clear`)
@jars creativedevtools
> tp P 1150.5 -60 1150.5
sleep 2
> execute as P at P run cdevbench passthrough
waitlog \[cdevbench\] passthrough: .* calls per case 300
sleep 2
shell python3 -c "import json;d=json.load(open('kubejs/exported/perf/passthrough_bench.json'));print({k:v for k,v in d.items() if k!='cases'});[print(c['id'],c['median_ns'],c['p99_ns']) for c in d['cases']]"
look tick_field and tick_web_cube medians under 1000; the two _recount rows present

## SQ-PS15B-22 | cdevreload compat picks up the new layer keys
@group A
@commands Rename-save `[surface.passthrough.layers] snowJumpLayers 8`, `thornChance 0`, `layersFall false`, then `/cdevreload compat`; restore
@pass each applies after the command (jump in snow 7 normal; no pricks; a snow layer over a removed stone breaks as vanilla); the client gets the re-sent table (sync format 4)
@fails `CompatConfigReload.reload`, `PassValues.FORMAT` 4, `LayerMotion` read from the config
@draft steps to write with SQ-PS15B-16 and -17

## CQ-PS15B-03 | leaf overlay inside a leaf pile; switch off
@group client
@commands First person inside an 8-layer oak leaf pile in a plains biome, then a birch pile (untinted), a 4-layer Twigs bamboo leaves pile, a full bamboo leaves 8; then `leafOverlay = false` and `/cdevreloadclient compat`
@pass oak: tiled oak leaves over the screen in the biome's foliage tint, about 0.7 opacity at 8 layers, lighter at fewer; birch: birch leaves; bamboo: Twigs bamboo leaves texture; off: no overlay; third person: no overlay
@fails `LeafOverlay.render` (IW `LeafPileBlock.getLeafType().leaves`, particle sprite, `BlockColors`), `RegisterGuiOverlaysEvent` registration
@draft client shots; `/cdevreloadclient compat` is a client command (see CQ-PS15B-02)

