## SQ-PS15B-23 | light mobs stand on snow layers 5, heavy mobs sink: rabbit, fox, chicken, cat, baby cow on top; cow, zombie, wolf, Alex's Mobs tiger in
@group A
@commands A 9 x 3 pen of snow layers 5 (x 1100 to 1108, z 1160 to 1162, fenced), one each of rabbit, fox, chicken, cat, baby cow (`{Age:-24000}`), cow, zombie (`{NoAI:0b}`, daylight-proof helmet), wolf, `alexsmobs:tiger`, all `{PersistenceRequired:1b}`; after 5 s read each mob's Y
@pass rabbit, fox, chicken, cat, baby cow: Y -59.375 (on top of 5 layers); cow, zombie, wolf, tiger: Y -60 (sunk to the ground); a zombie in leather boots (`armor.feet`) stands on top
@fails `SnowLayers.standsOn` / `light` (`snowLightVolume`, tag `creativecompat:snow_layer_light`, boots `canWalkOnPowderedSnow`), `SnowLayers.collision`; a tiger on top = `#minecraft:powder_snow_walkable_mobs` still read
@draft per-mob Y readback (`data get entity @e[type=...,limit=1] Pos[1]`) to write at the run

## SQ-PS15B-24 | a sunk mob climbs out of snow layers 7 onto a 1-block step and a snow block
@group A
@commands A cow and a zombie in a 1 x 4 trench of snow layers 7 sunk to the ground, a stone step 1 high at the trench end and a snow block at the other; lure: a player holding wheat for the cow, a survival bot for the zombie; then `snowMobClimb = false` (rename + `/cdevreload compat`) and repeat; restore
@pass on: both reach the top of the step (Y -59 on the stone) and the snow block within 10 s, rising at about 0.2 blocks per tick while touching the block; off: they stay in the trench (a 0.63 hop does not clear the step)
@fails `SnowMobMixin` (LivingEntity `handleRelativeFrictionAndCalculateMovement` RETURN), `SnowLayers.mobMove` / `sunkIn` (feet below the layer top), `snowMobClimb`
@draft per-tick Y watch of the mob to write at the run

## SQ-PS15B-25 | pathing over snow layers: a fresh mob plans over the top, a sunk mob plans through
@group A
@commands A villager (plain and MCA) and a zombie 10 blocks from a target across a 5 x 5 field of snow layers 6: path readback (`/cdevtest` path dump or the debug path renderer) before entering; then the same mobs placed sunk inside the field (summoned at ground level in the snow) with a new target across; then `snowSunkPathing = false` and repeat the sunk case
@pass outside: the first path's nodes over the field are one block up (on top of the snow); sunk: the path's nodes run at the ground level through the snow, the mob reaches the target without standing still; a mob that walks in on an over-the-top path gets a new ground-level path within about 1 s of sinking; off: the sunk mob keeps planning over the top (may stall at the field edge)
@fails `SnowPathMixin` (NodeEvaluator `prepare` / `done`), `SnowLayers.openForPath` in `LeafPilePathMixin` and `McaLeafPilePathMixin`, `SnowLayers.collision` (null-entity context while a sunk search runs), `SnowLayers.dropStalePath` (`recomputePath`)
@draft path readback to write at the run (no path dump verb yet: watch the mob's Y and position for 20 s)

