@@sources feature_writeup/plan_post_scratch_1115.md feature_writeup/plan_post_scratch_1115b.md feature_writeup/creative_devtools.md
@@text
@@text Creative Common build/libs 2026-11-17, not installed: Common watches our own mods' config files in `config/` (MODIFY
@@text and CREATE, 1 s debounce) and reloads them the way Forge does; night-config's watch on those files is removed.
@@text Headless: `tools/test_config_watcher.sh` ALL 23 OK. Every save below is made with no command; the copies are
@@text restored at the end of each row (a restore is itself a save and logs one reload line).
@@text
@@table
## SQ-PS15B-26 | in-place and rename saves of an own toml apply about 1 s later without a command, one reload each
@group A
@commands Boot line `config watcher on`; Compat `[debug.passthrough] timing` true by an in-place save (truncate + write, count 2: Forge missed it), then false by `sed -i` (rename); one appended blank line to Common's toml (a single write: Forge's own watcher would also have fired)
@pass boot: `[creativecommon] config watcher on: N own config file(s)`; each save gives exactly one `[creativecommon] <file> reloaded` line within 3 s; `[passthrough-timing]` lines start after the first save and stop after the second; one line (not two) for Common's append
@fails `OwnConfigWatcher.start` (FileWatcher.removeWatch, register MODIFY + CREATE), `OwnConfigLogic.Debounce`, `ConfigReload.reload` dispatch to the owning mod
@reviewed 2026-11-17
bootexpect \[creativecommon\] config watcher on: [0-9]+ own config file
shell cp config/creativecompat-common.toml .ps15b26_compat.toml
shell cp config/creativecommon-common.toml .ps15b26_common.toml
shell python3 -c "p='config/creativecompat-common.toml';s=open(p).read().replace('timing = false','timing = true',1);f=open(p,'r+');f.write(s);f.truncate();f.close()"
waitlog \[creativecommon\] creativecompat-common.toml reloaded 10
> cdevtest tickwarp 400
waitlog verb=tickwarp end=done ticks=400 120
waitlog \[passthrough-timing\] side=server 30
shell sed -i 's/timing = true/timing = false/' config/creativecompat-common.toml
sleep 4
> say ps15b26 after rename save
> cdevtest tickwarp 401
waitlog verb=tickwarp end=done ticks=401 120
shell printf '\n' >> config/creativecommon-common.toml
sleep 4
count \[creativecommon\] creativecompat-common.toml reloaded == 2
count \[creativecommon\] creativecommon-common.toml reloaded == 1
shell cp .ps15b26_compat.toml config/creativecompat-common.toml
shell cp .ps15b26_common.toml config/creativecommon-common.toml
sleep 4
reject reload failed
look `[passthrough-timing]` lines appear during the 400-tick warp and none after the `ps15b26 after rename save` line; the two counts above were taken before the restore

## SQ-PS15B-27 | loop guard: a touch reloads nothing, a corrected value reloads once (no loop); third-party tomls not touched by Common
@group A
@commands `touch` Compat's toml; then a wrong value `timing = "maybe"` saved in place (Forge-style correction: backup, fix to the default, save); then one appended blank line to a third-party toml (JEI's or Quark's, whichever exists in config/)
@pass touch: no reload line within 4 s; bad value: exactly one `[creativecommon] creativecompat-common.toml reloaded (1 value(s) corrected)` line and no second line within 5 s (the correction save is not reloaded again), the file reads `timing = false` and a `.bak` copy exists; third-party save: no `[creativecommon]` line for that file
@fails `OwnConfigLogic.ContentGuard` (`OwnConfigWatcher.noteApplied` after the save), `OwnConfigLogic.isOwn`
@reviewed 2026-11-17
shell cp config/creativecompat-common.toml .ps15b27_compat.toml
shell touch config/creativecompat-common.toml
sleep 4
> say ps15b27 touch done
shell sed -i 's/timing = false/timing = "maybe"/' config/creativecompat-common.toml
waitlog \[creativecommon\] creativecompat-common.toml reloaded \(1 value\(s\) corrected\) 10
sleep 5
shell grep -c 'timing = false' config/creativecompat-common.toml; true
shell sh -c 'f=$(ls config/jei-client.toml config/quark-common.toml 2>/dev/null | head -1); cp "$f" .ps15b27_third.toml; printf "\n" >> "$f"; echo "ps15b27 third=$f"'
sleep 4
count \[creativecommon\] creativecompat-common.toml reloaded == 1
reject \[creativecommon\] (jei-client|quark-common)\.toml
shell sh -c 'f=$(ls config/jei-client.toml config/quark-common.toml 2>/dev/null | head -1); cp .ps15b27_third.toml "$f"'
shell cp .ps15b27_compat.toml config/creativecompat-common.toml
sleep 4
look no reload line between the touch and `ps15b27 touch done`; the grep printed 1; a `creativecompat-common-*.bak` file was written by the correction (delete it after the run)

## CQ-PS15B-04 | client: an own toml saved by rename while the client runs applies without a command
@group client
@commands Client running (singleplayer): `sed -i` sets `[changelog] pauseButton = false` in `config/creativecommon-common.toml`; open the pause menu after 3 s; restore and reopen
@pass the client log has one `[creativecommon] creativecommon-common.toml reloaded`; the pause menu has no changelog book button after the save and has it again after the restore
@fails `OwnConfigWatcher` on the client (start at load complete), `ChangelogButtons` reading `pauseButton` live
@reviewed 2026-11-17
shell cp config/creativecommon-common.toml .cqps15b04_common.toml
key Escape
sleep 1
shot before
key Escape
shell sed -i 's/pauseButton = true/pauseButton = false/' config/creativecommon-common.toml
sleep 3
key Escape
sleep 1
shot off
key Escape
shell cp .cqps15b04_common.toml config/creativecommon-common.toml
sleep 3
key Escape
sleep 1
shot restored
key Escape
expect \[creativecommon\] creativecommon-common.toml reloaded
look shot before and restored: book button right of Back to Game; shot off: no book button
